      "message": "Actually I added an abstract method to QosFilter for this feature. However API rules doesn\u0027t allow adding a new abstract method to abstract class, and presubmit verification was failed.\n~~~~~~~~~~~\nerror: Added method android.net.QosFilter.matchesProtocol(int) [AddedAbstractMethod]\nAborting: Found compatibility problems checking the public API\n~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nSo, I queried this to api-council.\nAnd I added method \u0027matchesProtocol(int)\u0027 that has default implementation in QosFilter based on suggestion from api-council.\nhttps://groups.google.com/a/google.com/g/android-api-council/c/_QucGTXeLLg",
