      "writtenOn": "2022-08-02T09:43:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, right : you can\u0027t make it abstract because there may be implementations of this abstract class anywhere that can see @SystemApi, and adding an abstract method would break binary compatibility with these.\n\nI think we really need a comment to explain this. Please add a // comment before this method to explain it\u0027s being added in U, and therefore can\u0027t be abstract lest it might break binary compatibility with existing @SystemApi clients.\n\nAlso : who will use this method ? If it\u0027s only platform code (e.g. QosCallbackTracker) then you can make it abstract and @hide, which will remove the issue.\n\nThe throw here is pretty scary ; it will crash something at runtime if ever called, and it\u0027s really hard to make sure it never happens. Case in point : this patch doesn\u0027t supply an implementation for the one extant subclass of it (QosSocketFilter).",
