      "writtenOn": "2022-07-28T03:26:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we should remove some duplication here. The simplest way is probably to just remove the Pair and have callers get the agent and the socket separately. This will be especially true if you address my comment on l.963, because then everything that\u0027s the same in these two functions become one line. Then you can have a helper to create either type of socket, and all your callers now have to if() into one of these two methods anyway.\n\nYou could also write :\n\n    private fun \u003cT\u003e setupForQosCallbackTesting(creator : () -\u003e T) : Pair\u003cTestableNetworkAgent, T\u003e {\n      val request \u003d ...\n      ...\n      val socket \u003d create()\n      when (socket) {\n        is Socket -\u003e qosTestSocket \u003d socket\n        is DatagramSocket -\u003e qosTestDatagramSocket \u003d socket\n      }\n      return agent to socket\n    }\n\n    private fun setupForQosSocket() \u003d setupForQosCallbackTesting {\n      assertNotNull(agent.network?.socketFactory?.createSocket()).also {\n               it.bind(InetSocketAddress(InetAddress.getLoopbackAddress(), 0))\n    }\n    private fun setupForQosDatagram() \u003d setupForQosCallbackTesting {\n      DatagramSocket(InetSocketAddress(InetAddress.getLoopbackAddress(), 0))\n    }\n\nThis gets rid of duplicated code, allows for easier expansion into more sockets, and lets you remove the `!!`s (and if you implement my suggestion from l.182 you can get rid of the when()). \nHowever I think it\u0027s more complex than just removing these two functions and have callers call createConnectedNetworkAgent().",
