      "writtenOn": "2022-07-28T03:26:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you find a way to avoid repeating all this code ? I think the current structure with the two unrelated types makes it a bit hard to encapsulate in a function, but you could create a small helper class.\n\nBut there might be a simpler way ; if you implement my suggestions above, you could probably have something like\n\n    val (agent, _) \u003d createConnectedNetworkAgent()\n    val socket \u003d when(proto) {\n      IPPROTO_TCP -\u003e createTestSocket()\n      IPPROTO_UDP -\u003e createDatagramTestSocket()\n      else -\u003e fail(\"unsupported protocol\")\n    }\n\nThis gets rid of the two socket vars and makes `socket` the closest supertype of Socket and DatagramSocket, which is Closeable, so you have only one `close()` call in l.1095 and you don\u0027t need it to be nullable.\nOn the minus side that means you have to cast it in l.1063, but you can do this in a very clear manner with\n\n    fun QosSocketInfo(agent: NetworkAgent, socket: Closeable) \u003d when (socket) {\n      is Socket -\u003e QosSocketInfo(agent.network, socket)\n      is DatagramSocket -\u003e QosSocketInfo(agent.network, socket)\n      else -\u003e fail(\"unexpected socket type\")\n    }\n    [...]\n    val info \u003d QosSocketInfo(agent, socket)\n\n(or if you prefer your current if() structure for that part, it\u0027s fine too).\n\nAt that point, the duplicated code is much smaller and can be kept.",
